---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Waitlist from '../components/Waitlist.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
const C = SITE.checker;
---
<Base title="Add a Free Art Checker to Your Print Shop Website" description="Embed the free OKtoPress art checker on your print shop website with an iframe, a script tag, or the WordPress plugin shortcode [oktopress].">
<div class="wrap narrow">
  <h1>Put the free art checker on your shop's website</h1>
  <p class="muted">Your customers check resolution and ink colours before they send art. Uploads go to the OKtoPress service inside the iframe and never touch your website's server.</p>
  <section id="embed"><h2>1. Create your free shop account</h2>
    <p>Sign up with your email, shop name and website. We email you a sign-in link (no password), and your dashboard gives you a ready-made snippet with your own Shop ID. The checker only loads on the websites you register.</p>
    <p><a class="btn" href={C + '/signup'}>Set up my free checker</a></p>
    <p class="muted">Already signed up? <a href={C + '/login'}>Sign in to your dashboard</a>.</p>
    <h2>2. Paste the snippet from your dashboard</h2>
    <p>It's an iframe that works almost anywhere (add <code>?accent=RRGGBB</code> to match your brand colour), plus a script tag for auto-height where scripts are allowed. On WordPress, install the OKtoPress Art Checker plugin and use the shortcode <code>[oktopress]</code> or the block.</p>
    <h2>3. See checks and leads</h2>
    <p>Your dashboard lists the last 30 days of art checks, and customers can send their report straight to you so you can quote it.</p>
  </section>
  <Waitlist />
</div>
</Base>
